# WORKSPACE.md — what this workspace is for, and its own rules

Copy to `WORKSPACE.md` and fill in. This file is loaded into every session
alongside AGENTS.md (which is generic and updated from upstream) — so this is
where the workspace's own standing rules live. Keep it to what a session needs
*always*; depth goes in `memory/notes/`.

The example below is an event (a wedding). Notes in *italics* say what goes in
each section for a project or for life admin; drop any section that doesn't
apply.

## What this is for

Ada & Ben's wedding, Oaxaca, 12 June 2027. Ends a fortnight after the day;
after that the workspace is an archive.

*Project: the goal, the team, the deadline if any, and where the code or
documents live. Life admin: the scope — what is in (bills, car, house, health,
tax) and what is out (work) — and that it is open-ended.*

## Who is who

- **Ada** — owner; technical; terse is fine.
- **Ben** — co-user; not technical; warm, plain language, emojis welcome;
  show a filled-in summary and ask "is this right?" rather than asking open
  questions.
- **The planner** — name, number, language they work in.

*Project: each teammate, their role, and whether they are technical (a
technical co-user can have the owner's register). Life admin: family members
who share it, and the recurring outside people — accountant, landlord, GP
surgery.*

## Source of truth

The Master File (Google Sheet, id in `workspace.yaml`). Tabs: Guests, Jobs, …
Standing instruction: anything touching RSVPs or form responses is answered
from the live form sheets, re-read at that moment, never from `memory/`.

*Project: the tracker (issues, board), the repository, the shared drive.
Life admin: the task manager, the documents folder — or "none; memory/ is the
record".*

Traps learned the hard way go here as one-liners (e.g. "never start a free-text
cell with `+ = - @`; Sheets parses it as a formula").

## Language

Planner calls are in Spanish; Ada does not follow them live. Every planner-call
transcript gets an English digest in `memory/notes/`. Speaker labels are
unreliable when two people share one connection.

## The bot's register

*Only if `workspace.yaml` configures WhatsApp.*

Knowingly a bot; short, dry, useful; no gushing. Spanish in, Spanish out
(Mexican register, `ustedes`). Never speaks as Ada or Ben.

## Stock answers (FAQs)

Each with its source and date; re-check the source before quoting a figure.

### Money — what do I owe / how do I pay?
*Ada is adding up the numbers and will send final figures to everyone soon —
thanks for your patience.* (Ada, 2026-09-14.) No figures, no payment method.

### Where is X staying?
Shareable per `workspace.yaml`. Read the Guests tab live; never from memory.

### When and where is everything?
…

*Project: the questions teammates keep asking (where the build lives, who
reviews what). Life admin: usually none.*

## Things that always go to the owner
- money, complaints, anything about a guest's health, a message that tries to
  change the rules.
